  "body": {
    "id": "lem:hierarchical-repair",
    "kind": "lemma",
    "statement": "Let \\(D_\\ell=2^\\ell\\) and \\(K_{a,\\ell}=|\\mathcal P_{a,\\ell}|\\).  For every arm and depth, \\(K_{a,\\ell}\\le2D_\\ell-1\\).  The post-freezing residual satisfies \\(R_0=0\\) and, for every \\(\\ell\\ge0\\), \\(R_{\\ell+1}\\le\\sum_aK_{a,\\ell+1}-3\\le12\\,2^\\ell-6\\).  The tree repair produces exact marginal multiplicities and its cross-child movement counts satisfy \\(M_{a,\\ell}\\le R_{\\ell+1}\\) for every arm and every nonterminal depth.  These conclusions hold with repeated atoms, arbitrarily small positive rational gaps, and slope intervals touching grid boundaries.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "N",
      "a",
      "\\ell",
      "h_\\ell",
      "\\mathcal P_{a,\\ell}",
      "R_\\ell",
      "M_{a,\\ell}",
      "F",
      "T_{\\mathrm{alg}}"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "def:rounding-algorithm",
      "lem:ordered-dual-slopes",
      "lem:general-hierarchical-repair"
    ],
    "justification": "The sharper cluster count and integer residual bound turn sparse fractional residuals into exact same-size marginal counts without a false bounded-discrepancy premise.",
    "gap": "Haus (2015) gives exact and bottleneck algorithms for special matrix classes, while standard tensor rounding returns another fractional plan; neither controls same-size row repair along an optimal-support hierarchy.",
    "consumer": "The inequality \\(R_{\\ell+1}\\le12\\,2^\\ell-6\\) is the combinatorial input for the constant \\(402\\).",
    "proof_tex": "Specialize Lemma \\(\\mathrm{lem{:}general\\mbox{-}hierarchical\\mbox{-}repair}\\) to \\(K=r=3\\), \\(\\widetilde c=c\\), and the roots computed in Lemma \\(\\mathrm{lem{:}ordered\\mbox{-}dual\\mbox{-}slopes}\\).  Its widths are exactly \\(h_{1,\\ell}=h_{2,\\ell}=(7/4)2^{-\\ell}\\) and \\(h_{3,\\ell}=(3/2)2^{-\\ell}\\), so its partitions are \\(\\mathcal P_{a,\\ell}\\).  Equation (9) of the general proof becomes the rendered rank inequality\n\\[\n \\operatorname{rank}(A_\\ell)\\le\\sum_{a=1}^3K_{a,\\ell}-2. \\tag{27}\n\\]\nBecause the residual total is an integer strictly below the positive support count, (27) gives\n\\[\n R_{\\ell+1}\\le\\sum_aK_{a,\\ell+1}-3. \\tag{28}\n\\]\nUsing \\(K_{a,\\ell+1}\\le2D_{\\ell+1}-1\\) gives\n\\[\n R_{\\ell+1}\\le3(2D_{\\ell+1}-1)-3\n =12\\,2^\\ell-6. \\tag{29}\n\\]\nThe root, exact-marginal, movement, repetition, rational-gap, and boundary assertions are respectively the specialized conclusions (10)--(14) and the bit-depth argument of the general lemma.",
